<article class="env-lemma" id="015D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/015D">Lemma <span data-tag="015D">13.16.5</span>.</a> Let $F : \mathcal{A} \to \mathcal{B}$ be a left exact functor between abelian categories and assume $RF : D^{+}(\mathcal{A}) \to D^{+}(\mathcal{B})$ is everywhere defined. Let $0 \to A \to B \to C \to 0$ be a short exact sequence of $\mathcal{A}$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
If $A$ and $C$ are right acyclic for $F$ then so is $B$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $A$ and $B$ are right acyclic for $F$ then so is $C$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $B$ and $C$ are right acyclic for $F$ and $F(B) \to F(C)$ is surjective then $A$ is right acyclic for $F$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> In each of the three cases </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to F(A) \to F(B) \to F(C) \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> is a short exact sequence of $\mathcal{B}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/0152" data-tag="0152">13.12.1</a> we obtain a distinguished triangle $(A[0], B[0], C[0], a, b, c)$ in $D^{+}(\mathcal{A})$. As $RF$ is an exact functor and since $R^ iF = 0$ for $i < 0$ and $R^0F = F$ (Lemma <a href="/tag/05TD" data-tag="05TD">13.16.3</a>) we obtain an exact cohomology sequence 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to F(A) \to F(B) \to F(C) \to R^1F(A) \to \ldots  \]
</div>
    <p>
       in the abelian category $\mathcal{B}$. Thus the lemma follows from the characterization of acyclic objects in Lemma <a href="/tag/015C" data-tag="015C">13.16.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>